      "output": "{\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The diff genuinely simplifies WorkflowHub (net -20,571 lines): historical-permit machinery (reopen, rebind, continuation, recovery, replay, invalidation, flow-reset, adjudication-correction, verify passing/failure publications) is removed, and review-flow identity is re-keyed to the current material revision plus live snapshot, so history is audit-only and cannot block ordinary continuation. Formal safety remains fail-closed: publish/accept still validate current facts and audit carriers, acceptance of a replacement attempt requires a fresh human confirmation, build-code completion now demands a semantic integration review (pass or verified closed resolution) instead of accepting an unavailable formal record, verify-code recomputes completion and AC coverage from current spec/plan/tasks artifacts and requires tests/review/quality-review snapshots to match the current tree, atomic writer contracts are preserved and made more honest, and the final-coverage/final-gates validators bind each AC to a fixed oracle plus a real Vitest execution report. Five stages, confirmation/authorization boundaries, independent review facts distinct from permissions, clean Runner/Skill release surfaces, and node_modules exclusion are all preserved. Findings are minor only.\",\"findings\":[{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"acceptance-criteria.md\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"The supplied acceptance-criteria.md is empty (0 bytes), so AC-01..AC-15 coverage can only be assessed structurally from current-facts.json and the 2-line spec.md diff, not against actual criterion text.\",\"root_cause\":\"The frozen packet ships a placeholder acceptance-criteria file while the real AC text lives in specs/workflowhub-complexity-governance-v2/spec.md, which is not included in the bundle.\",\"recommendation\":\"Populate acceptance-criteria.md with the current AC list (or include the full spec.md) so independent reviewers can verify the coverage mapping, not just its shape.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"current-facts.json\",\"line\":49,\"issue\":\"final_gates.summary.formal_status says 'current-tree facts bound; final coverage validator pending' while final_gates.status is 'passed', missing_required_commands is empty, and all 15 final_coverage items are 'covered' with bound executions — internally inconsistent supplied facts.\",\"root_cause\":\"Stale narrative string in the final-gates summary left over from an earlier, genuinely pending state.\",\"recommendation\":\"Regenerate or correct the summary text so the formal status wording matches the passed gate and covered coverage record.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"core/stage-handlers.mjs\",\"line\":1212,\"issue\":\"verify-code computes the expected AC set as taskContract.facts?.ac_coverage?.accepted_ids ?? []; a missing ac_coverage silently degrades to an empty set, replacing the removed explicit failure ('accepted build-code lacks acceptance_coverage'). If both the contract AC set and the evidence criterion set were empty while the spec declares ACs, the mismatch check could not fire.\",\"root_cause\":\"The historical accepted-build cross-check was replaced by a current-contract read with a lenient default instead of an explicit absence check.\",\"recommendation\":\"Push an explicit mismatch when ac_coverage is absent or empty while the spec declares acceptance criteria, so the AC-set comparison stays fail-closed independent of contract internals.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"core/stage-handlers.mjs\",\"line\":397,\"issue\":\"certifyBuildCodeQualityBasis now skips the exact claimed-vs-actual diff match whenever claimedChanges is empty (pathOnlyCompletionClaim filters prose actual_changes to []), and the executed_commands binding is waived when a fresh test receipt is bound; tasks.md prose claims are no longer cross-checked against the authenticated diff.\",\"root_cause\":\"Deliberate relaxation so current runtime-authenticated receipts are authoritative and historical task-row copies cannot create stale self-references.\",\"recommendation\":\"Keep the implementation receipt as sole authority (as implemented), but document in the build-code contract that prose actual_changes are descriptive-only, or retain an optional warning when declared planned-boundary paths diverge from the diff.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"tests/workflow-v2-contract.test.mjs\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"Many concrete falsifiable assertions on the five stage SKILL.md files (steps.json step sequence, verify six-action repair handoff, human-brief content, per-Phase review command bindings) were replaced by loose keyword regexes, reducing the falsifiability of the stage-skill documentation contract.\",\"root_cause\":\"The workflow SKILL.md files were rewritten much smaller, so the old wording-level contract no longer matched and was replaced by presence checks.\",\"recommendation\":\"Re-anchor a small set of structural assertions (e.g., required gate/confirmation sections per stage) on the rewritten SKILL.md files so the contract test can fail on meaningful regressions, not just missing keywords.\"},{\"severity\":\"minor\",\"path\":\"docs/architecture/move-map.json\",\"line\":null,\"issue\":\"Several modules the diff now imports (runtime/review/review-policy.mjs, integration-review-subject.mjs, phase-review-subject.mjs, review-controller.mjs, review-output.mjs, schema-validator.mjs, core/task-capability.mjs, runtime/evidence/acceptance-evidence-validator.mjs) are recorded as moves but have no diff --git entries, so their current content is not reviewable from the frozen bundle.\",\"root_cause\":\"changes.diff was generated without rename/new-file detection for the moved review-layer files, and the packet does not embed their post-move contents.\",\"recommendation\":\"Include moved/created file contents (or rename-aware diff entries) in future review packets so the moved code, not just its call sites, is reviewable.\"}]}"
